summary:
  The heal ladder guards on isPlaying() instead of the listener's intent, so a
  parked station is healed back into playing with nobody asking.

history:
  2026.35 closed the engine side of this: a parked relay no longer re-arms at
  its window cap, and a late player error no longer rebuilds over a park. But
  the guard lives where the ENGINE declines, and main.qml reads that decline as
  "not a relay fall — try healing instead". The heal road then asked isPlaying()
  at four sites. A parked station is not playing, so all four let it through,
  the directory lookup ran, and startWithFade brought the room back. Reported by
  OdinVex on #13 as "pause, and it resumes anywhere from a few minutes to an
  hour later, repeatedly" — the second half of the same complaint, still open
  after 2026.35. Measured 2026-09-18 by tracing pause -> tap death -> error ->
  healTimer -> _tryHealStation -> _orderSubject -> _healAdvance -> audio, with
  no intent check anywhere on the path.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
      function _recoveryWanted() {
          return root._wantsPlaying && !root._tsPaused && !root._casting;

replace:
      function _recoveryWanted() {
          return root._wantsPlaying && !root._casting;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_every_automatic_recovery_road_asks_the_intent_not_the_state.
  Line-neutral.
